## 13. System-Level Guarantee

Given:

* Bounded disturbance
* Bounded neighbor injection
* Deterministic computation
* Feasible actuator authority

Distributed Safety Shields prevent cascade propagation by ensuring that no node can transition from safe to unsafe in a single update step.

